
## sync · plan
rc=0
🌲 git grove sync --mode plan
   ├─ ✗ grove-dead — its grove is no tailnet peer: a dead or replaced box
   │  └─ fix, once you confirm it is dead: git grove del grove-dead
   ├─ + grove-new — declares hetzner.hetzbot; would register grove-new and grove-new.ground
   ├─ ? grove-other — a grove peer with no entry, whose platform it did not declare (read: 'no answer')
   │  ├─ ssh said: camper@grove-other: Permission denied (publickey).
   │  └─ an ec2 grove registers by its tag: git grove set grove-other --exid <tag> --env <env>
   └─ to write: git grove sync --mode apply

## sync · apply
rc=0
🌲 git grove sync --mode apply
   ├─ ✗ grove-dead — its grove is no tailnet peer: a dead or replaced box
   │  └─ fix, once you confirm it is dead: git grove del grove-dead
   ├─ + grove-new — declares hetzner.hetzbot; registered grove-new and grove-new.ground
   │  └─ next, once you confirm the tailnet names this box: rhx git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-new --mode apply --trust tofu
   ├─ ? grove-other — a grove peer with no entry, whose platform it did not declare (read: 'no answer')
   │  ├─ ssh said: camper@grove-other: Permission denied (publickey).
   │  └─ an ec2 grove registers by its tag: git grove set grove-other --exid <tag> --env <env>
   └─ each row above with a fix is a human's call

